{"seconds": 54.0, "exit": 0, "final": "Excellent! White wins a queen (9 points) and is up significantly. So the main line is:\n\n**1. Ndc6+ Nxc6 (or bxc6/Qxc6) 2. Rxd5 Qxe5 3. Bxe5**\n\nAnd White wins material decisively. This is a **fork** pattern - after Ndc6+, both Black knights (on d5 and a5) are attacked and loose.\n\nNow let me write the coaching note:\n\n---\n\n**Best move: Ndc6+**\n\n**Main line:** Ndc6+ Nxc6 Rxd5 Qxe5 Bxe5\n\n**Motif:** fork\n\n**Explanation:**\nThe knight on d5 is undefended and attacked by your rook. When you play Ndc6+, you give check while forking two loose Black pieces: the d5 knight (attacked by your rook) and the a5 knight (attacked by your knight on c6). After any recapture of your knight, you capture the d5 knight with Rxd5, winning material. This is a knight fork that exploits the weakness of an undefended piece\u2014always scan for loose pieces that your forcing moves can exploit.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Ndc6+\", \"line\": [\"Ndc6+\", \"Nxc6\", \"Rxd5\", \"Qxe5\", \"Bxe5\", \"Nxe5\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "r2k3r/pppb1ppp/5q2/n2nN3/3N1B2/8/PPP1BPPP/3R1RK1 w - - 4 16"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "r2k3r/pppb1ppp/5q2/n2nN3/3N1B2/8/PPP1BPPP/3R1RK1 w - - 4 16"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r2k3r/pppb1ppp/5q2/n2nN3/3N1B2/8/PPP1BPPP/3R1RK1 w - - 4 16", "square": "d1"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r2k3r/pppb1ppp/5q2/n2nN3/3N1B2/8/PPP1BPPP/3R1RK1 w - - 4 16", "square": "f1"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r2k3r/pppb1ppp/5q2/n2nN3/3N1B2/8/PPP1BPPP/3R1RK1 w - - 4 16", "square": "e5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r2k3r/pppb1ppp/5q2/n2nN3/3N1B2/8/PPP1BPPP/3R1RK1 w - - 4 16", "square": "f4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r2k3r/pppb1ppp/5q2/n2nN3/3N1B2/8/PPP1BPPP/3R1RK1 w - - 4 16", "square":